        "title": "Recover evidence from partially failed fetch batches",
        "body": "When a fetch batch mixes usable text with failures, retain successful downloads by URL and track failures separately; exclude failure sentinels from extraction evidence. Inventory unresolved entity-field pairs after extracting and validating the usable evidence. For each remaining gap, inspect cached text first, then search for and fetch a relevant alternative source. Search snippets are leads, not substitutes for fetched proof. Do not repeat the entire successful portion of a batch or treat retrieval failure as evidence that a fact is absent. Validate the replacement quote against its fetched source and confirm that it supports the complete requested value before closing the gap. A failed URL need not eventually succeed when another verified source resolves the claim.",
